cial_summary":["Real REMAX Group Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $406M market cap on $2.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +73% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -444% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 9% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $62M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -15.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 24% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"SGA costs surged 32% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 23% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Real Estate peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"R